  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 491.71,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 461.33,
      "end": 491.69,
      "text": "The Friday Rock Show with Tommy Vance. Featuring sessions and tracks from artists including AC, Motörhead, Syd Barrett, Pretenders, Todd Rundgren. This is Tommy Vance on Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 491.71,
      "end": 494.53,
      "text": "some people who wrote in to me from New Mosley Head,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 494.59,
      "end": 496.31,
      "text": "the New Mosley Head Bangers, they call themselves,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 496.49,
      "end": 499.23,
      "text": "and they say, please play some music for Doudzee,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 499.31,
      "end": 500.63,
      "text": "that's Bill Ward, otherwise,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 500.89,
      "end": 502.49,
      "text": "also Robin, that's Terry Butler,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 502.89,
      "end": 505.67,
      "text": "Kenny, otherwise known as Anzee, it looks like, anyway,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 505.99,
      "end": 509.33,
      "text": "also Evil Aram, I wish I could read your writing properly,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 509.87,
      "end": 511.37,
      "text": "Jimmy, otherwise known as Mad Mel,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 511.55,
      "end": 513.11,
      "text": "and John, otherwise known as Tony.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 513.11,
      "end": 515.13,
      "text": "That's very interesting, weird names.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 515.49,
      "end": 516.95,
      "text": "And all the New Mosley Head Bangers,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 517.25,
      "end": 518.79,
      "text": "and the best-looking one, Liz,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 518.95,
      "end": 521.07,
      "text": "so hello, Liz, this is for you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 521.71,
      "end": 530.11,
      "text": "I reckon they knew it was going to be hot when they recorded that.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 951.01,
      "end": 953.93,
      "text": "That is Mama's Boys in session for this programme tonight",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 953.93,
      "end": 955.75,
      "text": "and the heat of the night.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 955.91,
      "end": 958.71,
      "text": "Mama's Boys, Pat, John and Tommy McManus",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 958.71,
      "end": 961.65,
      "text": "and Phil Begley on organ as well, thanks to them.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 962.15,
      "end": 965.61,
      "text": "Three more very strong tracks from one of the best bands from Ireland",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 965.61,
      "end": 967.31,
      "text": "coming up later in the programme.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 968.09,
      "end": 969.49,
      "text": "Coming up now on the programme,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 969.61,
      "end": 973.07,
      "text": "one of the most requested bits of live music ever featured on the show,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 973.07,
      "end": 976.37,
      "text": "recorded at the Hammersmith Odeon back in 1979.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 976.37,
      "end": 979.65,
      "text": "Stand by your radios for the Enid",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 979.65,
      "end": 982.65,
      "text": "What a beautiful recording",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 982.65,
      "end": 2052.01,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2052.01,
      "end": 2054.65,
      "text": "That's the Enid and God Save the Queen",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2054.65,
      "end": 2055.77,
      "text": "followed by The Last Judgment",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2055.77,
      "end": 2058.35,
      "text": "and then in the region of Summer Stars",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2058.35,
      "end": 2060.33,
      "text": "18 minutes of good music and another",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2060.33,
      "end": 2062.17,
      "text": "18 minutes coming up a bit later",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2062.17,
      "end": 2064.27,
      "text": "Between now and then we also have the",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2064.27,
      "end": 2066.11,
      "text": "Friday Night Connection, it's Richard Skinner",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2066.11,
      "end": 2067.87,
      "text": "for Tommy Vance on the Friday Rock Show",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2067.87,
      "end": 2070.43,
      "text": "at 22 minutes before 11 o'clock",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2070.43,
      "end": 2072.59,
      "text": "Going back some 18 minutes",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2072.59,
      "end": 2074.25,
      "text": "or more, I should have given a mention",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2074.25,
      "end": 2076.13,
      "text": "to a track by Aldo Nova called",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2076.13,
      "end": 2078.11,
      "text": "Heart to Heart, which we played before that",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2078.11,
      "end": 2080.27,
      "text": "Mama's Boys track. So anyway, my apologies",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2080.27,
      "end": 2081.61,
      "text": "for not telling you what that was earlier.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2081.99,
      "end": 2084.63,
      "text": "Some letters here. First of all from Tim Chamberlain",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2084.63,
      "end": 2085.91,
      "text": "of 8 Croft Close,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2086.05,
      "end": 2087.83,
      "text": "Moor Lane, Roughton in Chester.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2088.37,
      "end": 2090.17,
      "text": "Tim would like me to say hi to",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2090.17,
      "end": 2091.75,
      "text": "Jimbo and Groovy Nick.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2091.91,
      "end": 2094.19,
      "text": "That's his brother, who's a bit hot on the classics.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2094.77,
      "end": 2096.21,
      "text": "So I hope, Nick, that you got",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2096.21,
      "end": 2097.61,
      "text": "into that, because I thought it was rather good.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2097.77,
      "end": 2099.83,
      "text": "And I hope Tim did as well. So hi to Jimbo.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2100.15,
      "end": 2102.33,
      "text": "And also Michael Blakeman wrote in",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2102.33,
      "end": 2104.11,
      "text": "from Royton, Oldham in Lancashire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2104.11,
      "end": 2106.27,
      "text": "at No. 7 Consort Avenue, actually, in Royden.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2106.81,
      "end": 2109.73,
      "text": "And he asked me to say hi to headbanging John Radcliffe,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2109.85,
      "end": 2112.07,
      "text": "Berg, the Mad Axeman, the Two Seers,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2112.45,
      "end": 2115.27,
      "text": "Ian Loverball Hall, Pip Palmer, and also himself.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2115.39,
      "end": 2117.03,
      "text": "Also, please give a mention, he says to everybody,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2117.59,
      "end": 2121.39,
      "text": "involved in O-level exams this year at North Chatterton School.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2122.03,
      "end": 2124.59,
      "text": "Yeah, do it as near to 10.30 as possible, he says.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2124.93,
      "end": 2126.63,
      "text": "It is done. Michael, thank you for the letter.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2127.15,
      "end": 2129.47,
      "text": "Hope you can headbang to a bit of ready, roundy California.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2129.63,
      "end": 2131.27,
      "text": "I think it might be a bit difficult, though, actually.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2132.13,
      "end": 2137.53,
      "text": "Mumma's Boys' Runaway Dreams, another track from their session.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2137.53,
      "end": 2740.42,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2745.42,
      "end": 2750.06,
      "text": "Before that, you heard Skull and Crossbones from Randy California's LP, Euro American.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2751.71,
      "end": 2753.33,
      "text": "10 to 11, Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2761.47,
      "end": 2764.45,
      "text": "Theme 1 by George Martin and played by Vandegraaff Generator",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2764.45,
      "end": 2766.47,
      "text": "introduces us, of course, to the Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2767.11,
      "end": 2770.79,
      "text": "Moving on from last week's Connection, which I thought was quite a difficult one",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2770.79,
      "end": 2773.83,
      "text": "because it was a little obscure, but the mail said otherwise.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2774.83,
      "end": 2779.11,
      "text": "We pulled a winner out, and the person who divined correctly the connection",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2779.11,
      "end": 2785.43,
      "text": "last friday was tommy woods congratulations tommy tommy wrote from 126 parkfield road great lever in",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2785.43,
      "end": 2790.61,
      "text": "bolton in lancashire and tommy was right he's not only a diamond head freak he's also the man who",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2790.61,
      "end": 2796.79,
      "text": "realized that the tracks we played which were the prisoner by iron maiden back in black from ac dc",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2796.79,
      "end": 2803.13,
      "text": "and lady evil by black sabbath all featured established bands with new vocalists first",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2803.13,
      "end": 2807.89,
      "text": "recordings of new vocalists iron maidens bruce bruce first recorded on the number of the beast",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2808.41,
      "end": 2811.35,
      "text": "Back in black, Brian Johnson with ACDC,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2811.53,
      "end": 2813.77,
      "text": "Ronnie James Dio and Black Sabbath from the LP",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2813.77,
      "end": 2815.91,
      "text": "Heaven and Hell on Lady Evil.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2816.61,
      "end": 2817.71,
      "text": "Tommy's sorted that out.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2818.01,
      "end": 2820.55,
      "text": "Your prize is on its way to you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2821.05,
      "end": 2822.69,
      "text": "And Tommy has also managed to put together",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2822.69,
      "end": 2824.07,
      "text": "another Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2824.13,
      "end": 2826.75,
      "text": "See if you can find out what gets this lot together.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2826.93,
      "end": 2828.75,
      "text": "And first of all, let's go back in time.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2829.25,
      "end": 2835.85,
      "text": "Time again for another of your favourite rock and roll sessions",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2835.85,
      "end": 3086.55,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3086.55,
      "end": 3089.27,
      "text": "as you enjoy the Moondog Show.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3089.89,
      "end": 3097.69,
      "text": "Five past eleven, and that is the end of the Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3677.33,
      "end": 3679.43,
      "text": "Or maybe it's just the beginning.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3681.42,
      "end": 3686.38,
      "text": "That connection's set by Tommy Woods from Great Leber in Bolton in Lanx.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3686.52,
      "end": 3686.96,
      "text": "Thanks, Tom.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3687.38,
      "end": 3689.78,
      "text": "Don't forget, if you think that you know the connection there,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3690.02,
      "end": 3693.68,
      "text": "and maybe it's not so hard after all, then do write down the connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3694.2,
      "end": 3697.64,
      "text": "Send the results of your connection to Tommy, who'll be here next Friday.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3697.64,
      "end": 3703.42,
      "text": "That's Tommy Vance, Friday Night Connection, Friday Rock Show, Radio 1, London, W1A, 4WW.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3703.98,
      "end": 3707.16,
      "text": "And don't forget to add your connection, too,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3707.26,
      "end": 3710.78,
      "text": "and hopefully your card or letter will be dragged out of that sack",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3710.78,
      "end": 3712.4,
      "text": "between now and next Friday.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3713.63,
      "end": 3716.37,
      "text": "Reminder of the address, it's the Friday Night Connection,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3716.47,
      "end": 3721.07,
      "text": "Friday Rock Show, Radio 1, London, W1A, 4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3722.15,
      "end": 3726.47,
      "text": "Coming up soon, more from the Enid, another 18 minutes,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3726.65,
      "end": 3728.51,
      "text": "an excellent thing called Fand...",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3728.51,
      "end": 3735.11,
      "text": "Myofist from their LP Thunder and Rock, and that's evil cold.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3735.11,
      "end": 4358.7,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4358.7,
      "end": 4362.22,
      "text": "Before that, another dose of the Mama's Boys, as I said earlier.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4362.42,
      "end": 4364.2,
      "text": "It makes it sound something rotten, which it wasn't.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4364.34,
      "end": 4366.4,
      "text": "And Belfast City Blues.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4366.76,
      "end": 4368.66,
      "text": "That's a track that I think they've had out as a single",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4368.66,
      "end": 4371.48,
      "text": "because we had it on the round table that we did from Belfast",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4371.48,
      "end": 4373.56,
      "text": "and an excellent bit of music too.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4375.02,
      "end": 4376.86,
      "text": "Coming up towards 16 after 11,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4377.12,
      "end": 4380.44,
      "text": "a bit of the Enid coming up after a few dedications that I'd like to read out.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4380.52,
      "end": 4382.64,
      "text": "First of all, an anonymous writer,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4382.72,
      "end": 4384.34,
      "text": "they're writing in indeed from Huddersfield,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4384.46,
      "end": 4385.96,
      "text": "says on the 4th of June,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4385.96,
      "end": 4388.22,
      "text": "could you please play a record for Dale Trenum,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4388.22,
      "end": 4390.56,
      "text": "who lives on Watterson Close in Mansfield.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4390.96,
      "end": 4392.98,
      "text": "It'll be his 14th birthday on the 4th.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4393.22,
      "end": 4396.28,
      "text": "Send him love and best wishes from a friend in Huddersfield.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4396.48,
      "end": 4398.2,
      "text": "Dale, you have a friend in Huddersfield",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4398.2,
      "end": 4400.0,
      "text": "and happy birthday for today.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4401.66,
      "end": 4407.92,
      "text": "Hi also to Chris Chaplin who wrote a line from Hutton in Essex",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4407.92,
      "end": 4411.36,
      "text": "and asked for a dedication for Kazzy and Lou at Reading University",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4411.36,
      "end": 4414.9,
      "text": "and all the other headbangers at the aforementioned establishment,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4415.4,
      "end": 4416.26,
      "text": "whether he knows them or not.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4416.58,
      "end": 4419.5,
      "text": "Also a special mention, please, for Paul Metal Mountie Wainwright",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4419.5,
      "end": 4422.88,
      "text": "who he reckons is the only metal mountie working in the city.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4423.0,
      "end": 4424.72,
      "text": "Chris, I wonder what a metal mountie is.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4425.2,
      "end": 4427.6,
      "text": "No doubt everybody else knows and are now laughing at me.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4427.76,
      "end": 4427.9,
      "text": "Right.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4429.3,
      "end": 4430.86,
      "text": "Carl Richardson, good evening to you too,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4430.94,
      "end": 4434.3,
      "text": "from Greenways Bridal Path, Ashback, Stoke-on-Trent in Staffordshire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4434.96,
      "end": 4438.34,
      "text": "Carl says, please say a big hello to my girlfriend, Rosemary Winship.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4438.72,
      "end": 4438.98,
      "text": "Hello!",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4439.82,
      "end": 4440.96,
      "text": "Hope that didn't wake you up too much.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4441.46,
      "end": 4444.42,
      "text": "Because, Rosemary, I gather that you are 18 on Sunday,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4444.66,
      "end": 4445.58,
      "text": "so that's a good one.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4445.7,
      "end": 4447.12,
      "text": "You just missed a few by-elections there,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4447.14,
      "end": 4448.48,
      "text": "but some voting coming up for you soon.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4448.48,
      "end": 4450.86,
      "text": "writing in there from 13 Uplandscroft,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4451.08,
      "end": 4452.16,
      "text": "Warrington, Stoke-on-Trent",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4452.16,
      "end": 4453.92,
      "text": "and happy birthday for Sunday to you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4454.94,
      "end": 4455.92,
      "text": "Oh, P.S. says Carl,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4456.1,
      "end": 4457.6,
      "text": "tell her mum that the cookies are ace.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4459.88,
      "end": 4461.22,
      "text": "And last but far from least,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4461.28,
      "end": 4462.62,
      "text": "as all the best disc jockeys say,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4462.7,
      "end": 4464.28,
      "text": "Janet Dawson, thank you for your note",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4464.28,
      "end": 4466.64,
      "text": "from 30B Green Street, Upton Park,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4466.84,
      "end": 4468.54,
      "text": "London, East 6th.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4469.58,
      "end": 4471.44,
      "text": "Please wish me a happy 21st birthday,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4471.58,
      "end": 4471.9,
      "text": "says Janet.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4472.0,
      "end": 4474.32,
      "text": "Happy 21st for the 7th of June to you, Janet.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4475.36,
      "end": 4477.02,
      "text": "And you'd like to hear Todd Rundgren",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4477.02,
      "end": 4478.96,
      "text": "from the new album A Swing to the Right.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4479.04,
      "end": 4480.3,
      "text": "We haven't got it in tonight's show,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4480.3,
      "end": 4482.56,
      "text": "but we have got it in tomorrow's Rock On.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4483.71,
      "end": 4485.97,
      "text": "So tune in, Radio 1 tomorrow night at 5.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4486.09,
      "end": 4487.21,
      "text": "We've got an interview with Todd,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4487.35,
      "end": 4489.29,
      "text": "plus some good music from that same album.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4489.83,
      "end": 4496.43,
      "text": "Yes, the Enid.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4496.91,
      "end": 4501.11,
      "text": "Just hear that applause, and well-deserved too.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5594.36,
      "end": 5597.98,
      "text": "The Enid from 1979, recorded at the Hammersmith Odeon,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5598.56,
      "end": 5600.22,
      "text": "and a track called Fanned.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5600.48,
      "end": 5602.92,
      "text": "Now, if you're into the Enid and that sort of sound,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5603.4,
      "end": 5604.76,
      "text": "that ain't the last you're going to hear of them either,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5604.82,
      "end": 5606.58,
      "text": "because my producer Tony Wilson tells me",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5606.58,
      "end": 5608.78,
      "text": "that the Enid have a Volume 2 tape,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5608.78,
      "end": 5611.88,
      "text": "Quotes coming out in the next four weeks",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5611.88,
      "end": 5613.86,
      "text": "So the Enid",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5613.86,
      "end": 5614.9,
      "text": "Still doing it",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5614.9,
      "end": 5616.5,
      "text": "And doing it very well as well",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5616.5,
      "end": 5618.28,
      "text": "Right a few more dedications",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5618.28,
      "end": 5620.76,
      "text": "Not now but after a couple more bits of music",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5620.76,
      "end": 5623.0,
      "text": "And in the meantime Doc Holliday is back",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5623.0,
      "end": 5625.24,
      "text": "Riding again in a hot rod",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5625.24,
      "end": 5628.24,
      "text": "Who else could it be",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5628.24,
      "end": 5935.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5940.0,
      "end": 6129.58,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6129.58,
      "end": 6131.58,
      "text": "Status Quo and their new single",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6131.58,
      "end": 6132.58,
      "text": "She Don't Fool Me",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6132.58,
      "end": 6134.28,
      "text": "Before that a bit of Doc Holliday",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6134.28,
      "end": 6135.2,
      "text": "Some American rock",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6135.2,
      "end": 6137.5,
      "text": "From the album Doc Holliday Rides Again",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6137.5,
      "end": 6138.64,
      "text": "You heard Hot Rod",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6138.64,
      "end": 6141.16,
      "text": "quarter to 12 exactly on the nose",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6141.16,
      "end": 6142.12,
      "text": "on the Friday Rock Show",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6142.12,
      "end": 6144.34,
      "text": "and that is time for me to say good evening to Mike",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6144.34,
      "end": 6146.74,
      "text": "at 45 Kingston Deverill Warminster",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6146.74,
      "end": 6149.04,
      "text": "in Wiltshire, that's where you get all those amazing",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6149.04,
      "end": 6150.6,
      "text": "flying saucers don't you Mike",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6150.6,
      "end": 6152.96,
      "text": "well good luck with the flying saucers",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6152.96,
      "end": 6155.2,
      "text": "also hi to your girlfriend Trudy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6155.2,
      "end": 6156.3,
      "text": "from Mere in Wiltshire",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6156.3,
      "end": 6159.34,
      "text": "Trudy, Mike reckons you're a very special lady",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6159.34,
      "end": 6161.6,
      "text": "so thank you from him for going with him",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6161.6,
      "end": 6164.37,
      "text": "also much more",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6164.37,
      "end": 6166.23,
      "text": "formal SF Alexander",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6166.23,
      "end": 6167.81,
      "text": "26 Little Stone Road",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6167.81,
      "end": 6169.39,
      "text": "Little Stunning Kent wrote in",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6169.39,
      "end": 6173.31,
      "text": "and asked me to say hello to Andy, Dean, Nigel, Pete, Willie",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6173.31,
      "end": 6175.03,
      "text": "and all Genesis freaks listening.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6175.35,
      "end": 6177.59,
      "text": "And SF Alexander, you ought to stick around",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6177.59,
      "end": 6180.53,
      "text": "because after our next track, the last one this evening from Mumma's Boys,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6181.05,
      "end": 6183.75,
      "text": "a bit of live Genesis from their new live LP.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6183.93,
      "end": 6184.99,
      "text": "That's coming up any time.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6185.63,
      "end": 6189.11,
      "text": "Also hi to Andy Smallwoods of Newton Abbey County and Trim",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6189.11,
      "end": 6192.29,
      "text": "who says please say hi to all the Monkstown area headbangers",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6192.29,
      "end": 6196.33,
      "text": "and play some Northern Ireland rock right now.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6196.51,
      "end": 6197.75,
      "text": "Here we go, Mumma's Boys.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    }
  ]
}